All of Milestone 5 is implemented and every test suite is green.

## What was built

**`app/src/main/java/com/daydreamvr/player/screens/widgets/`**

| File | Contents |
|---|---|
| `WidgetGeometry.kt` | `PixRect` (pure rect value type) + `Bands` band-budget constants |
| `SourceSidebarWidget.kt` | Header + vertical 3-row source switcher + divider + measured folder list; `visibleRows()` = exact fitting-row count |
| `MediaGridWidget.kt` | Derived 3×2 grid, 6 cards/page, 16:9 posters, badges/duration/watched bar, **whole-card** hit region, absolute `GridCell(page*6+slot)` index |
| `MediaInspectorWidget.kt` | Bottom-anchored `PLAY` / `RESUME` / `Projection` actions, top-down poster+title+metadata clipped where it would collide with the action block |
| `SystemDockWidget.kt` | 6 equal cells tiling `[0,672)`, one `DockButton` hit region per cell |

Each widget takes `(theme, metrics, measure)`, exposes a pure `measureLayout(model, bounds)`, a `draw(...)`, and `hitRegions(layout): List<HitRegion<GazeTarget>>`, mirroring `ListView`.

**Deviation from the prompt (necessary):** the signature says `bounds: RectF`, but `android.graphics.RectF` is a no-op stub under `unitTests.isReturnDefaultValues = true` (verified: constructor does nothing, fields read `0f`), which would make every layout assertion vacuous. Widgets take/return `PixRect` and convert to `RectF` only inside `draw`, on-device — the same "plain floats in the pure path" approach `ListView` already uses.

**`vrcore/.../Theme.kt`** — added `badgeVr` / `badge3d` / `badgeQuality` (plan §4).

